-- הסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011), §56 הסכמי מסגרת במגזר הציבורי: the cost of
-- framework agreements the New General Histadrut signs with the State or the
-- public employers up to 31.12.2016 is applied to the teaching employees
-- too, by those agreements' terms and dates, subject to a collective
-- agreement between the parties; failing agreement on how within 90 days
-- of a framework agreement's signing, by a uniform rise of the teachers'
-- salary tables at its cost.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `oz-founding-common`

§ `56 הסכמי מסגרת במגזר הציבורי`

-- ¶1, the first sentence: the cost of the framework agreements signed, if
-- any are, between the New General Histadrut and the State and/or the
-- public employers in the period to 31.12.2016 (the day included:
-- convention dates.end) is applied, by the conditions and dates those
-- agreements set, to the teaching employees (§4(א)) too, "בכפוף לחתימה
-- על הסכם קיבוצי בעניין זה בין הצדדים להסכם זה".
@ref akn:art_56/p1
`the last day a framework agreement section 56 reaches is signed` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2016

GIVEN `signed between the Histadrut and the State or the public employers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `signed on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a framework agreement section 56 reaches` `signed between the Histadrut and the State or the public employers` `signed on` IF
        `signed between the Histadrut and the State or the public employers`
    AND `signed on` `is on or before` `the last day a framework agreement section 56 reaches is signed`

`section 56's first sentence makes the cost's application subject to a collective agreement` MEANS TRUE

-- ¶1, the second sentence: if the parties do not agree how the cost is
-- applied to the teaching employees within 90 days of the framework
-- agreements' signing (the 90th day in: convention dates.end), it is
-- applied by raising the teachers' salary tables at a uniform rate by the
-- cost.
--
-- F-oz-founding-56-a: the first sentence makes the application subject to
-- the parties' collective agreement, and the second gives a way to apply
-- the cost where they have not agreed, without saying whether it too waits
-- for one. The reading adopted (convention precedence.specific): the
-- second sentence, which speaks of the case where the parties did not
-- agree, applies the uniform rise without a further agreement.
@ref akn:art_56/p1
`the days section 56 gives the parties to agree` MEANS 90

DECLARE `how section 56 applies a framework cost` IS ONE OF
    `as the parties' collective agreement sets it`
    `not yet decided`
    `by a uniform rise of the teachers' salary tables at the cost`

GIVEN `days since the framework agreement was signed` IS A NUMBER
      `the parties agreed how, in a collective agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `how section 56 applies a framework cost`
DECIDE `how a framework cost is applied under section 56` `days since the framework agreement was signed` `the parties agreed how, in a collective agreement` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the parties agreed how, in a collective agreement` THEN `as the parties' collective agreement sets it`
        IF `days since the framework agreement was signed` AT MOST `the days section 56 gives the parties to agree` THEN `not yet decided`
        OTHERWISE `by a uniform rise of the teachers' salary tables at the cost`

`section 56's second sentence asks a collective agreement for the uniform rise` MEANS FALSE

`why the framework agreements are not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "הסכמי מסגרת שייחתמו, ככל שייחתמו, בין ההסתדרות הכללית החדשה לבין המדינה ו/או המעסיקים במגזר הציבורי עד 31.12.2016"

§§ `56 -- illustrations`

#ASSERT `a framework agreement section 56 reaches` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2016)
#ASSERT NOT `a framework agreement section 56 reaches` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2017)
#ASSERT `how a framework cost is applied under section 56` 90 FALSE EQUALS `not yet decided`
#ASSERT `how a framework cost is applied under section 56` 91 FALSE EQUALS `by a uniform rise of the teachers' salary tables at the cost`
#ASSERT `how a framework cost is applied under section 56` 200 TRUE EQUALS `as the parties' collective agreement sets it`

-- F-oz-founding-56-a's evidence: the first sentence asks a collective
-- agreement, the second does not, and the encoding applies the uniform
-- rise with none signed.
`section 56 asks a collective agreement in one sentence and not in the other` MEANS
        `section 56's first sentence makes the cost's application subject to a collective agreement`
    AND NOT `section 56's second sentence asks a collective agreement for the uniform rise`
    AND `how a framework cost is applied under section 56` 91 FALSE EQUALS `by a uniform rise of the teachers' salary tables at the cost`
#ASSERT `section 56 asks a collective agreement in one sentence and not in the other`
